@page "/docs/components/vekdatagrid/filtering"
@layout DocumentationLayout

<PageTitle>VekDataGrid Filtering | Vek Components</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-page-layout">
    <article class="docs-article">
        <h1>VekDataGrid: Filtering</h1>
        <p class="docs-intro">Search across selected columns, combine quick predicates with per-column filters, and choose a filter surface.</p>

        <section id="live-example" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="live-example-heading">
            <h2 id="live-example-heading">Live example</h2>
            <p>Search product names and categories, or choose a filter layout and enter a value to narrow the products.</p>
            <div class="filter-mode-picker" role="group" aria-label="Filter layout">
                <button type="button" class="@ModeClass(VekDataGridFilterMode.Simple)" aria-pressed="@(_filterMode == VekDataGridFilterMode.Simple ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => SetMode(VekDataGridFilterMode.Simple)">Panel</button>
                <button type="button" class="@ModeClass(VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnMenu)" aria-pressed="@(_filterMode == VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnMenu ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => SetMode(VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnMenu)">Column menu</button>
                <button type="button" class="@ModeClass(VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnRow)" aria-pressed="@(_filterMode == VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnRow ? "true" : "false")" @onclick="() => SetMode(VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnRow)">Filter row</button>
            </div>
            @if (_products is null)
            {
                <p class="docs-loading" role="status">Loading sample products...</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="docs-example-frame">
                    <VekDataGrid TItem="DemoProduct" Items="_products" PageSize="10"
                                 FilterMode="@(_filterMode == VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnRow ? VekDataGridFilterMode.Simple : _filterMode)"
                                 ShowFilterRow="@(_filterMode == VekDataGridFilterMode.ColumnRow)">
                        <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Name" Title="Name" Searchable="true" Filterable="true" FilterOperator="VekDataGridFilterOperator.Contains" />
                        <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Category" Title="Category" Searchable="true" Filterable="true" FilterOperator="VekDataGridFilterOperator.Contains" />
                        <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Price" Title="Price" Format="C2" Filterable="true" FilterOperator="VekDataGridFilterOperator.GreaterThanOrEqual" />
                    </VekDataGrid>
                </div>
            }
        </section>

        <section id="code" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="code-heading">
            <h2 id="code-heading">Code</h2>
            <p>Columns can select their comparison operator, and the grid applies filters before sorting and paging.</p>
            <VekCodeViewMulti Tabs="_codeSamples" />
        </section>

        <section id="filter-modes" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="filter-modes-heading">
            <h2 id="filter-modes-heading">Filter modes and operators</h2>
            <p><code>Simple</code> places controls above the grid, <code>ColumnMenu</code> groups each control in a menu, and <code>ColumnRow</code> places controls below the headings. Use <code>FilterBy</code> for a custom selector, <code>FilterTemplate</code> for a custom editor, and <code>FilterCaseSensitive</code> to set string matching behavior.</p>
            <p>Available operators include equality, text matching, numeric comparisons, and null or empty checks. Filter changes reset the page and are exposed through <code>CurrentState</code> and <code>FilterChanged</code>.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="global-search" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="global-search-heading">
            <h2 id="global-search-heading">Global search</h2>
            <p>The search field matches text across columns marked <code>Searchable="true"</code>. Set <code>SearchColumnKeys</code> on the grid to choose an explicit target set, or provide <code>SearchBy</code> on a column to search a derived value.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="filter-options" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="filter-options-heading">
            <h2 id="filter-options-heading">Filter properties</h2>
            <p>Filtering is opt-in per column. Set <code>Filterable="true"</code> on the columns users can filter, then choose where their controls appear with <code>FilterMode</code>.</p>
            <dl class="filter-property-list">
                <div>
                    <dt><code>Filterable</code> <span>bool</span></dt>
                    <dd>Enables filtering for this column and includes it in the chosen filter surface.</dd>
                    <dd class="property-default">Default: <code>false</code></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><code>FilterBy</code> <span>Func&lt;TItem, object?&gt;?</span></dt>
                    <dd>Selects the value compared by filters. If omitted, filtering uses the value selected by <code>Property</code>.</dd>
                    <dd class="property-default">Default: <code>null</code></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><code>FilterOperator</code> <span>VekDataGridFilterOperator</span></dt>
                    <dd>Sets the comparison used by the built-in editor, such as <code>Contains</code> or <code>GreaterThanOrEqual</code>.</dd>
                    <dd class="property-default">Default: <code>Contains</code></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><code>FilterTemplate</code> <span>RenderFragment&lt;VekDataGridFilterContext&gt;?</span></dt>
                    <dd>Replaces the built-in editor with custom controls that can apply or clear this column's filter.</dd>
                    <dd class="property-default">Default: built-in editor</dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><code>FilterMode</code> <span>VekDataGridFilterMode</span></dt>
                    <dd>Chooses the filter surface: <code>Simple</code>, <code>ColumnMenu</code>, or <code>ColumnRow</code>.</dd>
                    <dd class="property-default">Default: <code>Simple</code></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><code>FilterCaseSensitive</code> <span>bool</span></dt>
                    <dd>Controls whether string comparisons distinguish uppercase and lowercase letters.</dd>
                    <dd class="property-default">Default: <code>false</code></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><code>QuickFilter</code> <span>Func&lt;TItem, bool&gt;?</span></dt>
                    <dd>Applies an item-level predicate before the per-column filters.</dd>
                    <dd class="property-default">Default: <code>null</code></dd>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <dt><code>FilterChanged</code> <span>EventCallback&lt;IReadOnlyList&lt;VekDataGridFilter&gt;&gt;</span></dt>
                    <dd>Notifies the parent when column filters are applied or cleared.</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </section>
    </article>

